{
  "id": "COMPOUND:42038 - PROTEIN:5867",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which (2E,4E)-N-isobutylundeca-2,4-dien-8,10-diynamide interacts with HaCaT cells. This compound is identified as a target for multiple enzymes in the SDR family, which are involved in the metabolism of various substrates. The evidence links the compound to Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which is subsequently targeted by two different metabolites: 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol and 6-Hydroxy-2-[2-(2-hydroxyphenyl) ethyl]chromone. Both of these metabolites are known to target HaCaT cells, indicating a possible pathway through which the compound may exert its effects. The integration of these targets suggests that the compound may act through a metabolic pathway involving SDR family enzymes, potentially modulating cellular processes in HaCaT cells. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between the compound and HaCaT, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
